    "notes": "1. Scale: All values are in millions (1E6) as indicated in the statement header. 2. Total Revenue: Composed of 'Product' and 'Service and other' line items. 3. Total Operating Cost: Includes all costs and expenses deducted from revenue to arrive at Operating Income. This comprises 'Cost of revenue' (split into Product and Service and other) and the three operating expense categories: Research and development, Sales and marketing, and General and administrative. 4. Taxes: 'Provision for income taxes' is used. 5. Interest Expenses: 'Interest expense' from the supplementary table for 'Other Income (Expense), Net' is used. The value is reported as a positive number as it is an expense that reduces income (per rule 13). 6. Other income/expense components (e.g., interest income, investment gains/losses) are not part of the requested normalized fields and are therefore excluded. 7. The 'Other, net' line within Other Income is not mapped as it is a miscellaneous catch-all not directly corresponding to a requested field.",
